# CODEOWNERS — who must approve when these files change
#
# The files listed here are the team's shared rules and agreements, the common
# baseline everyone works from. Changes can still be proposed through a PR as
# usual, but need the file owner's approval before merge, so the shared rules
# never change without the team agreeing.
#
# ⚠️ Branch protection "Require review from Code Owners" must also be turned on
#    for both main and dev — this file alone enforces nothing.
#
# To add your own commands/guidelines for Claude Code, put them in
# .claude/commands/<name>.md, which .gitignore already excludes — it never
# reaches git and doesn't affect the team's CLAUDE.md. See the personal
# guidelines section in CLAUDE.md.

# The team's shared working rules
/CLAUDE.md              @cha130y

# Requirements and architecture documents
/docs/requirements/     @cha130y
/docs/architecture/     @cha130y
/docs/team-role/        @cha130y

# The shared schema every module uses — don't change it without agreeing first
/apps/api/prisma/       @cha130y

# CI and workspace config
/.github/               @cha130y
/package.json           @cha130y
/pnpm-workspace.yaml    @cha130y

# API dependencies — adding/removing a package changes the whole team's tech
# stack (CLAUDE.md: "don't change the tech stack without asking") and everyone
# has to pnpm install again. This file used to have no owner, even though the
# root /package.json did.
/apps/api/package.json  @cha130y
